    - { name: "Field Armorer & Munitions Expert", base: 50, per_level: 5, note: "Metal Working (Special): a basic understanding of smithing, particularly weapons and jewelry. Equal to the Field Armorer skill with a +10% bonus." }
    - { name: "Gemology", base: 35, per_level: 5, note: "Recognize Precious Metals & Stones: same as the Gemology skill with a +10% bonus." }
    - { name: "Language: Dwarven", base: 98, per_level: 0, note: "Speak, read and write the traditional Dwarf language at 98%. The book gives the languages to 70% of Dwarves." }
    - { name: "Language: Dragonese", base: 80, per_level: 5, note: "Dragonese/Elven +30%. 70% of Dwarves." }
natural_abilities:
  - name: "Nightvision"
    description: "90 feet (27.4 m)."
  - name: "Underground Tunneling (Special)"
    description: "Dig and build solid, strong tunnels with no fear of a cave-in, and excavate ruins and cave-ins with the same prowess. Can usually tell whether a tunnel or chamber is natural or was dug by Dwarves, Kobolds, Goblins, Gnomes, Troglodytes or humans, and whether it is new, old or ancient. Base Skill: 40% +5% per level of experience."
  - name: "Underground Architecture"
    description: "Build rooms, archways, staircases, great vaulted chambers and labyrinths of tunnels, mazes and underground traps (usually pit and cave-in traps); recognize Dwarven, Kobold, Goblin and other construction. Travelling slowly and cautiously, a Dwarf can locate traps and avoid or deactivate them. Base Skill: 30% +5% per level; trap detection and deactivation at half the architecture skill."
  - name: "Underground Sense of Direction"
    description: "Tell direction underground even in total darkness (not on the surface): up, down or level, the approximate angle, depth below the surface and compass direction. Base Skill: 40% +5% per level. Judging the location of surface structures in a familiar area: 30% +5% per level, -25% in an unfamiliar area."
  - name: "Technical Aptitude"
    description: "A natural aptitude for weapon design, mechanics, building and manufacturing gives +5% to all Mechanical, Military, Electrical and Computer skills. Apply by hand."
  - name: "S.D.C. Mortal"
    description: "No natural A.R. and no M.D.C. - a Dwarf needs M.D.C. body armor, a force field or magic. Most prefer medium to heavy armor, up to full environmental and power armor. No Horror Factor."
restrictions:
  - "O.C.C.s: any, including equivalents of the CS or Triax military. Leans toward Operators, City Rats, Rogue Scientists (especially electrical and mechanical engineering) and Men of Arms. Most magic O.C.C.s can be considered, but 99% of Dwarves avoid the mystic arts; the few who practice choose Techno-Wizardry, Stone Magic or Conjuring, and the evil and daring perhaps Bio-Wizardry, Necromancy, Summoning or Shifting."
extraction_notes: |
  - Rifts Conversion Book One printed 84-86 (file p085-p087). The Rifts conversion of the Palladium Fantasy Dwarf, which is the `dwarf` row. A separate class because a variant cannot cross systems.
  - S.D.C. is 20 here - "20, plus those gained from O.C.C.s and physical skills" - where the Palladium Fantasy row carries 15. Stored as a POOL BONUS.
  - "+1 to save vs magic" is one printed line and lands on all five magic save keys, as on the Palladium row. The split is the app''s, not the book''s.
  - Metal Working and Recognize Precious Metals & Stones are grants, at the catalog base plus the printed +10%, as on the Palladium row.
  - "Special Skills of Note" gives the Dwarf language at 98% and Dragonese/Elven (+30%) to 70% of Dwarves; granted, with that on each line. Literacy in Dwarven is part of the 98% line ("speak, read and write"), and the catalog''s Language: Dwarven row is spoken only, so reading it is prose.
  - NOT MODELLED: the Tech Note''s +5% to all Mechanical, Military, Electrical and Computer skills. A per-skill modifier on skills the OCCUPATION grants, which a race cannot state. Prose.
  - No occ_restrictions: the Rifts line allows any O.C.C. The Palladium row''s `except: group:magic` does NOT carry over - on Rifts Earth the book allows a magic O.C.C. and says only that almost no Dwarf takes one.
  - Psionics: "Standard, same as humans", so no psionics block.
  - Size three feet plus 3D4+2 inches; weight 150 to 200 pounds; life span 250+ years, some to 500. In the Lore.
  - The section-wide rule on printed 74 - a new arrival from the Palladium World picks up the regional language and two Modern W.P.s within weeks, then three Rifts skills from Communications, Pilot (basic vehicles), Technical and W.P. Modern after 2D4+4 months or one level, and one more language or skill every two levels - applies to a character who came from Palladium rather than one raised on Rifts Earth. It is not stored; the survey carries it.
